From dab915a38b575c6cb274eeeef9f730ee12fe1c88 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ch0mpaa <christian.gonzalez@infosystemsinc.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 22:05:41 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] qwen27 CUDA: keep and resume prompt states in the shared
 prompt cache

The qwen27 CUDA family had no snapshots, so the server ran it with no prompt cache and every
request re-read its whole prompt. reuse.zig copies a stream's committed state (DeltaNet
recurrences and conv windows, and the attention caches' first at rows) and restores it; a pass
with the cache in play cuts the zero-anchored grid so kept states line up. cuda.zig now takes
each family's own snapshot functions instead of Nemotron's. Cache-off passes are unchanged.

Gate: offsec-v1 greedy answers are token-identical with the cache on and off; follow-up questions
on a 79K-token prompt resume from 77,824 cached tokens (75 s to 1.7 s).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
